---
import { siteHref } from '../../lib/site';
import { Code } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';

import ReferencePage from '../../components/ReferencePage.astro';

const commitGrammar = '[(i/N) ][TICKET] type(scope)!: description';
const hookCommand = 'repo-standards commit-message .git/COMMIT_EDITMSG --fix-safe';
const textCommand = 'repo-standards pull-request text PR_BODY.txt';
---

<ReferencePage
  title="Git policies"
  description="Commit-message, PR text and history policies outside the repository rule registry."
>
  <article class="git-policies">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Version-control contracts</p>
      <h1>Git policies</h1>
      <p class="lede">Commit messages, PR text and history are checked outside the repository rule registry. They are commands and hooks, so they do not appear in the rule count.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="git-policy-grammar" aria-labelledby="commit-header-grammar">
      <p class="eyebrow">Commit header grammar</p>
      <h2 id="commit-header-grammar"><code>{commitGrammar}</code></h2>
      <p>The optional series marker comes first, followed by an optional ticket, a conventional-commit type, optional scope and breaking marker, then a concise description.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="capability-grid git-policy-grid">
      <section class="capability-card" aria-labelledby="compact-pr-descriptions">
        <p class="data-line">PR text · advisory preflight</p>
        <h2 id="compact-pr-descriptions">Preview a compact description</h2>
        <p>Check a UTF-8 body file before publishing. Default budgets allow 500 rendered prose characters and 2,000 total characters, including links, comments and automation markup.</p>
        <Code code={textCommand} lang="bash" frame="terminal" wrap />
        <p>Link detailed evidence and retain the outcome, validation and material caveats. Nonempty, closed code fences need a language tag.</p>
        <p>Warnings exit zero. Unreadable, oversized or invalid input exits two. This preview uses default budgets; the configured review-policy check remains authoritative.</p>
        <p>The shared pull-request commit action runs this advice automatically on PR events, including metadata edits. It emits warnings without changing the PR or the commit-policy verdict.</p>
        <p>Pass <code>--title</code> to preview a title. Descriptive subjects above 72 characters receive advice. Recognized ticket, series, type and scope prefixes and trailing <code>(#123)</code> or <code>(GH-123)</code> references do not spend that target.</p>
        <p>PR titles may also start with <code>gh-123:</code> or <code>bpo-123:</code>, optionally after a branch label such as <code>[3.14]</code>. These prefixes do not spend the target. GitHub reference spelling is case-insensitive.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="capability-card" aria-labelledby="managed-commit-headers">
        <p class="data-line">commit-msg · local and CI</p>
        <h2 id="managed-commit-headers">Managed commit headers</h2>
        <p>The hook validates new commit headers. Safe fixing normalizes only casing and spacing; commit bodies and trailers remain untouched.</p>
        <p>The shipped commit hook includes subject-length advice; standalone calls opt in with <code>--advise</code>. Advice preserves strict syntax results and message bytes. Keep essential identifiers even when the subject needs extra space.</p>
        <Code code={hookCommand} lang="bash" frame="terminal" wrap />
        <p>CI validates every direct non-merge commit, including commits created before a contributor installed the hook.</p>
        <p><a href={siteHref("/cli/#commit-message")}>Commit-message command reference</a></p>
      </section>

      <section class="capability-card" aria-labelledby="reviewable-pr-history">
        <p class="data-line">pull-request history · CI authoritative</p>
        <h2 id="reviewable-pr-history">Reviewable pull-request history</h2>
        <p>Pull requests may contain up to five direct commits by default. Longer histories must use a complete, ordered <code>(1/N)</code> through <code>(N/N)</code> series.</p>
        <p>The local hook is advisory because it cannot know the final base and head refs. CI evaluates the direct commits in the submitted pull request.</p>
        <p><a href={siteHref("/cli/#pull-request.commits")}>Pull-request commit command reference</a></p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</ReferencePage>
